{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>לאחד</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ככה תעשו לאחד כמספרם. Each one's meal-offering was one tenth [of an ephah] and the lamb that comes with the omer — its meal-offering was two tenths. And it is found in the Midrash: one tenth for the single lamb, the remainder for the Holy One, blessed be He, for He is One. And so too: תעשו לאחד כמספרם — just as you made for the lamb, so shall you make one extra tenth for the 135."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The final abbreviation הקכ\"ה / הקב\"ה appears twice: once as the standard reverent form for 'the Holy One, blessed be He,' and once at the very end as a number (135). The latter is likely a gematria or masorah count, but the Hebrew as given reads identically; I have translated the first instance as the divine reference and the second as the number 135, preserving both exactly as they appear."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:15.334943304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}